<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- IOS-1b-A R603/R605. The shared design system finds these ten Lucide drawables BY NAME at run time
     (shared design/Glyph.android.kt), which R8's resource shrinker cannot see - so they are kept here by name.
     The list is asserted against the Glyph enum by GlyphDrawablesExistTest, so a glyph added to the enum and not
     to this file fails a test rather than shipping blank.

     shrinkMode="strict", MEASURED, not assumed: in the default "safe" mode a run-time name lookup makes the shrinker
     keep, defensively, every resource it cannot rule out - 68 more than main's release APK (every ic_* drawable, and
     androidx core's notification and compat resources), +33,004 bytes. In strict mode the release APK's resource
     table names EXACTLY main's 197 resources (aapt2 dump, diffed both ways: empty) and the APK is 12 bytes larger.
     Strict mode keeps what is referenced from code or listed here; nothing in this app looks a resource up by name
     except Glyph.android.kt, whose names are this list.
     IOS-2a R767: eight more (the onboarding kit's glyphs and the ones its callers hand IconCircle) - each was
     referenced from :app code as R.drawable before the kit moved, so main kept it already; listed now because the
     only reference left is the run-time name.
     IOS-MOVE-CORE R1300: three more - the bottom bar's (sun, calendar, settings), referenced from :app as R.drawable
     until AppBottomBar moved to :shared commonMain and drew them through Glyph. -->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:shrinkMode="strict"
    tools:keep="@drawable/ic_building_2,@drawable/ic_house,@drawable/ic_briefcase,@drawable/ic_plane,@drawable/ic_calendar_x,@drawable/ic_clock,@drawable/ic_circle_check,@drawable/ic_triangle_alert,@drawable/ic_circle_x,@drawable/ic_octagon_alert,@drawable/ic_chevron_left,@drawable/ic_info,@drawable/ic_logo_mark,@drawable/ic_mail,@drawable/ic_calendar_check,@drawable/ic_file_text,@drawable/ic_lock,@drawable/ic_bell,@drawable/ic_sun,@drawable/ic_calendar,@drawable/ic_settings" />
